WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.440
I will not say when we are going to attack,
but attack we will.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:13.360
They will be met with fire and fury like the
world has never seen.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.900
It's almost nine months into Donald Trump's
presidency

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.240
and I've got a question specifically for the
old "Libertarians for Trump" crowd:

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.040
How much more winning can you take?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.020
I urge all of my fellow Americans to stand
up and vote for Donald Trump.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.180
There was a small but vocal band of limited-government
folks

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.140
who supported the billionaire real estate
mogul

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.600
on the grounds that he couldn't possibly be
as bad as Hillary Clinton

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.980
or even most of the other Republican candidates,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.079
especially when it came to foreign policy.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.800
I personally have had to put aside my Libertarian
beliefs to support Trump....

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.980
I think that I won the debate, is because
of his inability or refusal

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.160
to rank Hillary and Donald...

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.180
Leading the pack was economist Walter Block,

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:59.530
who beat me in a competitive debate in New
York City right before the election,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.680
on whether or not Libertarians should support
Trump.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.720
Block’s argument was that “the perfect
is the enemy of the good”

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.640
and “the Donald is the most congruent with
[the libertarian] perspective”

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.440
especially on foreign policy.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.820
But Trump has turned out to be anything but
a non-interventionist.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.400
He promised to bring fire and fury to North
Korea,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.400
“the likes of which, in this world has never
seen before.”

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.720
He bombed Syria on the same humanitarian grounds
he explicitly denounced during his campaign.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.620
He escalated war efforts in Yemen and Iraq,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.220
and more recently, announced plans to "win"
in Afghanistan.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.099
His secretary of state declared that

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.360
the US might not walk away with a "battlefield"
victory in the graveyard of empires,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.600
but neither would the Taliban.

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:46.700
That’s not inspirational, it’s stupid.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.749
Apart from his foreign policy follies,

00:01:48.749 --> 00:01:50.539
this anti-free-trader and nativist

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.700
has turned out to be even less libertarian
than advertised during the campaign.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.340
They're rapists and some, I assume are good people.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.600
White lives matter!

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.060
He’s continued giving mealy-mouthed support
to white supremacists

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.200
and pardoned Joe Arpaio, "America's toughest
sheriff,"

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.480
who was found in contempt of court after he
continued to illegally racially profile

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.560
and detain Latino suspects.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.320
Nobody is higher than me.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.360
And Trump's attorney general Jeff Sessions

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.780
is walking back a decade of incremental progress
on criminal justice reform.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.480
Trump's deregulatory push is all to the good,

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.860
but it’s overwhelmed by his other
policies.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.159
And there's also no question

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:32.129
that at this point Trump is doing virtually
everything he can do to alienate libertarians

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:35.870
who believe in shrinking the size, scope,
and spending of government.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.020
Donald, what do you think of Libertarianism?

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.220
I like it, a lot of, a lot of good things.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.700
I don't wanna talk to you now, but a lot of
good things, a lot of good points.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.600
The excuse that Hillary Clinton would have
been worse is getting older than Bernie Sanders.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.859
The perfect is the enemy of the good

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.680
but what the president has shown us so far
just isn’t good enough.

